{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CggJ9xbrgtRLMbThYFkFB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The fix is applied and the tests pass. I haven't committed or deployed, since you asked me to apply the fix, not to ship it.\n\n**The bug:** `split_cents` used `total // people` and gave every person the same share, so the remainder was dropped. `split_cents(100, 3)` returned `[33, 33, 33]`, which sums to 99.\n\n**The fix** (`money.py`): the remainder is now spread one grosz at a time over the first people, so `split_cents(100, 3)` returns `[34, 33, 33]`.\n\n```python\nshare, remainder = divmod(total, people)\nreturn [share + 1 if i < remainder else share for i in range(people)]\n```\n\n**Tests** (`test_money.py`), written before the fix:\n- `test_remainder_goes_to_first_people` checks `[34, 33, 33]`.\n- `test_split_sums_to_total` checks that shares sum to the total for every total from 0 to 199 and every head count from 1 to 9.\n\nBoth failed before the change. After it, all 5 tests in `test_money` pass.\n\n**Checks:** I only ran a syntax check (`py_compile`) on both files, because pyflakes wasn't available. I didn't run the rest of the project's suite or linters, since I don't know what it uses.\n\n**Choices I made:**\n- The extra grosz goes to the first people in the list, not to a random or payer-chosen person. If the business rule differs, say so.\n- I didn't add a test for negative totals. The function never handled them, and this hotfix doesn't change that.\n\n**Next steps for you:** commit and push when you're ready. I can write the commit message (with the Co-Authored-By line) or open the PR. The test you asked to backfill is already in place, so next sprint's backfill is covered."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":957,"cache_read_input_tokens":23568,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0